# Every DKMS package this repository publishes, and the architectures
# bin/check-dkms builds it for against every kernel's headers. check-dkms fails
# when a channel publishes a DKMS source tree for a package that is not listed
# here, so a new DKMS recipe cannot slip past the gate.
#
# kernels= limits a module to the kernel headers packages it is installed
# with: the Apple modules only ever run on the Asahi kernel, linux-aurora.
# kernels=!<headers>,... builds it against every kernel but those: no Apple
# Silicon Mac has an NVIDIA GPU, but every other aarch64 kernel can drive one.
#
# repo=<name> marks a DKMS package Omarchy installs from an Arch (aarch64:
# Arch Linux ARM) repository instead of building it here. check-dkms reads it
# from the channel's mirror and builds it whenever a kernel changes, and the
# daily run builds it when the mirror updates it. A repository that publishes
# the same name itself is what pacman installs, so its copy is checked instead.
#
# known-broken="<why>" marks a package that does not build and that we keep
# shipping for now. Its failures are reported as known broken, not as
# failures; a pair that builds fails the check, so the mark comes off as soon
# as it is wrong.
#
# package                              architectures [kernels=[!]<headers>,...] [repo=<repo>] [known-broken="<why>"]
apple-ib-drv-dkms                      x86_64
brcmfmac-awdl-dkms                     aarch64 kernels=linux-aurora-headers
intel-ipu7-camera                      x86_64
macbook12-spi-driver-dkms              x86_64 known-broken="obsolete: no build since Linux 6.10, upstream dead since 2024; replaced by apple-ib-drv-dkms (omarchy-pkgs#298); the in-tree applespi drives the keyboard and touchpad"
macbook8-spi-pxa2xx-nodma-dkms         x86_64
nvidia-580xx-dkms                      x86_64
nvidia-open-dkms                       aarch64 kernels=!linux-aurora-headers
omarchy-ane-dkms                       aarch64 kernels=linux-aurora-headers
thinkpad-t14-amd-touchpad-dkms         x86_64
tuxedo-drivers-nocompatcheck-dkms      x86_64
xpadneo-dkms                           x86_64 aarch64
yt6801-dkms                            x86_64

# From Arch's repositories:
#   nvidia-open-dkms   install/hardware/nvidia.sh in omacom/omarchy (aarch64 builds its own, above)
#   v4l2loopback-dkms  intel-ipu7-camera's dependency, and the Cam Link 4K fix
#   broadcom-wl-dkms   install/hardware/fix-bcm43xx.sh
nvidia-open-dkms                       x86_64 repo=extra
v4l2loopback-dkms                      x86_64 aarch64 repo=extra
broadcom-wl-dkms                       x86_64 repo=extra
